WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
Cut your finger, and within days
the gap fills with brand-new

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:04.930
cells.

3
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:05.930
Not muscle.

4
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:06.970
Not bone.

5
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.150
Exactly the right kind of cell,
in exactly the right place.

6
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.230
So where do the new cells come from,

7
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.750
and how does a cell end up
as skin rather than muscle?

8
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.430
In this mission, you'll see
a cell copy its DNA before it

9
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.090
divides.

10
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.030
You'll watch mitosis make two
genetically identical cells,

11
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.930
for growth and repair.

12
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.930
And you'll meet stem cells,

13
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.110
which can become other
types of cell, in embryos,

14
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.230
in bone marrow and in plant meristems.

15
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.730
Your mission: find out
where new cells come from.
